      "input_intro": {
        "buggy": "Incident: index-warning classification is inconsistent with the migration's table operations.\n\nThe analyser examines literal SQL; this investigation does not connect to a database. Non-concurrent index creation on an existing table must retain its warning. An index on a table created in the same migration should be exempt, and this must hold when a migration indexes several tables. Preserve the other analyser rules and concurrent-index behavior.\n\nA capture containing `CREATE TABLE \"films\" (\"title\" text);` followed by `CREATE INDEX ON \"films\" ((lower(\"title\")));` reports `CREATE_INDEX`. The same index without a corresponding table creation must continue to warn. The snapshots below are the code under investigation.\n",
        "changed-defect": "Incident: index-warning classification is inconsistent with concurrent operations.\n\nThe analyser examines literal SQL; this investigation does not connect to a database. Non-concurrent index creation on an existing table must retain its warning. An index on a table created in the same migration should be exempt, and this must hold when a migration indexes several tables. Preserve the other analyser rules and concurrent-index behavior.\n\nThe current capture reports `DROP_INDEX` for `DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY ON films;`, but gives no warning for `DROP INDEX ON films`. The snapshots below are the code under investigation.\n"
      },
